WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:28.600
The experiment of sending kids back to school
during a raging hundred year pandemic by this

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:35.140
administration has failed and it has failed
very poorly.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.520
And I'm not pleased to see this.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:41.530
And to be clear, I wish it were possible to
send kids back to school safely right now.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:45.910
It's become very popular among some on the
right to say the left wants to hurt businesses.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:47.860
The left wants to hurt education.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.449
The left wants it left, doesn't care about
people's emotional health, all because they

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:54.880
want to close, close, close in order to hurt
Donald Trump.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:01:02.370
I don't deny for a second that there are tangible
benefits, intangible benefits and psychological

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.530
benefits to getting kids back to school.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:09.020
I don't deny that many parents can't get back
to work unless their kids are back in school.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:10.300
So I get it.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.750
The considerations are economic.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:12.770
They're emotional.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:14.219
They're wide ranging.

00:01:14.219 --> 00:01:16.790
When you have 50000 cases a day.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:19.420
Fourteen hundred deaths a day.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:24.119
And we've already debunked the false notion
that kids can't catch the disease or spread

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:25.460
the disease.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.270
It just doesn't pass the sniff test that this
would work.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:34.020
And case in point, a Georgia second grader
tested positive on day one back in school.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.560
By day two, the classroom was closed.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.090
The teacher and students were quarantined
for two weeks and out of school.

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:46.130
And there are many of these examples, 260
employees either tested positive or were exposed

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.250
in Gwinnett County public schools in Georgia.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.240
That's Georgia's largest school district.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.719
Hours after the first day in an Indiana district
last week, the County Health Department notified

00:01:56.719 --> 00:02:01.609
Greenfield Central Junior High that a student
who had been in a bunch of classrooms all

00:02:01.609 --> 00:02:07.459
over the school in contact with teachers and
students helped was helping students.

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:09.369
I don't remember the exact details was all
over.

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:12.470
The school tested positive for Corona virus.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:17.180
And once again caused a mass quarantine of
14 days for everybody that they had been in

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.260
touch with.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:23.140
We saw what happened in Israel where they
successfully dealt with the virus, crushed

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.140
the curve.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.680
I mean, just obliterated it, obliterated the
curve, opens schools.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.250
And then things went backwards very, very
quickly.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:37.320
So it's not inconceivable that states could
open schools.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.920
Some states could open schools safely, maybe.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.870
But a lot has to happen in order to do that.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:47.740
First and foremost, when we were down to 20000
cases a day.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:49.060
Every state started opening.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.800
That was not the time to actually start opening
as aggressively as happened.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:58.520
Number two, I know that it's August, but we
still don't have enough testing or fast enough

00:02:58.520 --> 00:02:59.520
testing.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.370
The testing is falling behind the viral spread
when we talk about how much we test relative

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:04.980
to other countries.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.800
Remember that at this point, circumstances
are so different in countries that in order

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:15.870
to keep up with our level of spread, we need
dramatically more testing and we need dramatically

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.120
faster testing.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:21.400
People are often not hearing back for days,
five to seven days in some cases.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:26.910
A travel blogger I know waited 20 days for
his test results, got them the day before

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.660
he was going to a different state.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:33.890
This is the same issue we've been talking
about for a long time when it comes to lots

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:38.760
of types of businesses and organizations and
certainly schools where people are even more

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.640
crowded together for hours all day.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.090
There is not an easy, easy answer.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.870
I am not pretending this is simple.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:48.160
I get all of the reasons why we would want
to open schools.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:54.040
But what we've seen so far, we have to be
guided by the data tells me the risks exceed

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.830
the possible rewards.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:04:02.450
By the spring semester early 2021, we might
have both more effective treatments and vaccines

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.600
that are increasingly inoculating people.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.780
So to me, that says let's do online in the
fall.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:07.780
I'm not saying don't do it.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.540
I'm saying let's do it online.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.540
Let's suffer through it.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.090
My mom is a college professor.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:15.480
Up until two days ago, they were planning
on allowing professors to teach in person

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.480
if they wanted to.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:17.480
Now, my mom.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.530
Already decided to go fully remote, but because
of what's happening now in Massachusetts,

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:25.600
which, by the way, is nothing compared to
what's going on in some states.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.940
Her university decided we're doing all remote.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:29.949
It sucks, but it makes sense.

00:04:29.949 --> 00:04:30.949
It's a mess.

00:04:30.949 --> 00:04:31.990
It's not political.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:32.990
Masks should be worn.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.180
It's not political.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:36.010
It's too early to open a lot of things.

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:37.310
It's not political.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:43.289
I'm so glad I'm not in a position of having
to send kids to school or not and make decisions

00:04:43.289 --> 00:04:44.800
about where they should be.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.129
I don't envy the parents.

00:04:46.129 --> 00:04:48.279
I don't envy the teachers or the administrators.

00:04:48.279 --> 00:04:49.600
I'm not pretending it's easy.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.600
I get it.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.720
There is not a simple answer, but it's increasingly
clear that the safe answer is you've got to

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.819
do online in the fall.

00:04:57.819 --> 00:05:01.580
And increasingly, it seems more and more states
are going in that direction.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.479
Let me know what's happening in your state.

00:05:03.479 --> 00:05:05.779
Let me know on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:05:05.779 --> 00:05:10.259
And remember, you can listen to the David
Pakman show podcast every day, every weekday,

00:05:10.259 --> 00:05:11.259
OK?

00:05:11.259 --> 00:05:18.880
We take weekends off on whatever your favorite
podcasting app is, Spotify, I, iTunes, Stitcher,

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:19.880
Pandora.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:20.880
It's quite a laundry list.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.120
It's almost too easy to get the audio podcast,
but I encourage you to do it.

